summary:
- topic: FY2027 Budget
  text: The board announced a public budget forum for what is expected to be a difficult
    FY2027 budget year, emphasizing the need for public input on creative cost-saving
    measures. The Finance Committee also reported a projected deficit for the current
    fiscal year.
- topic: Superintendent Search
  text: The board formally approved a contract with Zeal Education Group to conduct
    the superintendent search. Additional funds were also approved for national advertising
    and for comprehensive background checks on finalists.
- topic: Community Safety and Equity
  text: The board and public expressed significant concern over recent ICE activity.
    The superintendent reaffirmed the district's commitment to safety for all students,
    and there were public calls for accelerated staff training and clearer public
    guidance to support vulnerable families.
- topic: Facilities
  text: An update was provided on the South Portland Middle School field, with a plan
    to aerate, overseed, and fertilize in the spring to make it playable by Fall 2026.
    The district maintains it will not pay for the remediation.
- topic: Policy
  text: The board approved the second reading of the School Board Member Ethics policy
    (BCA) and accepted the first reading of a revised Public Participation at Board
    Meetings policy (BEDH).
- topic: Graduation Plans
  text: Due to the athletic complex construction, the SPHS graduation for the class
    of 2026 will be held offsite at the Cross Insurance Arena. The board discussed
    the logistics and costs, including providing parking vouchers for families.
- topic: School Calendar
  text: A vote on the 2026-2027 school calendar was postponed to February to allow
    for negotiations with the service employees union regarding the impact of an additional
    contracted school day.
- topic: Personnel
  text: The board accepted several resignations and announced retirements for the
    end of the school year, including educators from Kaler Elementary, the middle
    school, and the high school.
